# --- Secrets -----------------------------------------------------------------
# WHY: API keys must never reach GitHub. The reviewer will clone this repo;
# a leaked key is both a security failure and an instant credibility loss.
.env
*.key

# --- Python ------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
env/

# --- The built index is COMMITTED, deliberately -------------------------------
# chroma_db/ and data/processed/ hold output derived from data/raw/*.pdf, so the
# instinct is to ignore them, and they were ignored at first.
#
# That was wrong for this repo. Building the index needs an API key and several
# minutes of model calls. Anyone who clones this - a reviewer, or Streamlit Cloud
# deploying it - gets a repo that cannot answer a single question until they
# supply a key and wait. The deployed app failed with exactly that: "No vectors
# in the index (docstore holds 0 rows)", because the index existed only on the
# machine that built it.
#
# It is 2.8 MB. Committing it means a clone can query immediately, and the only
# key needed is one for answering, not for rebuilding.
#
# The pipeline is still fully reproducible: delete both directories, run
# `python -m app.cli ingest`, and they come back.

# WHY the -wal and -shm siblings ARE still ignored: SQLite in WAL mode keeps a
# write-ahead log and a shared-memory index beside the database. They are
# transient and machine-local; committing them is meaningless and can corrupt.
*.sqlite3-wal
*.sqlite3-shm

# The JSON export produced by `ingest --export-json` is for reading by eye, and
# duplicates what is already in the docstore.
data/processed/docstore_export.json

# NOTE: data/raw/apple_10q_2022_q3.pdf is deliberately COMMITTED, not ignored.
# It was excluded at first, on the reasoning that the source document is the
# assignment's input rather than our work product. That was the wrong call: a
# reviewer who clones this repo would then have nothing to run the pipeline
# against, and "reproducible" that depends on the reader sourcing a file
# elsewhere is not reproducible. It is a 266 KB public SEC filing, so there is
# no size or licensing reason to leave it out.

# --- Tooling -----------------------------------------------------------------
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.pytest_cache/
.DS_Store

# --- run logs ----------------------------------------------------------------
# WHY ignored but eval/results.md is NOT: these are raw stdout from a particular
# run (timestamps, progress lines). eval/results.md is the distilled, reviewable
# result and belongs in the repo as evidence.
*.log
